00:44:15.665 --> 00:44:32.999
Same thing is true for a woman on the other side of that. So a sociologist named Prentice Tipton a number of years ago did a study particularly in the African-American community because the African-American community was having a major breakdown in the family.

00:44:32.999 --> 00:45:10.425
A lot of dads in 1950s the African-American families were strong men and women together raising kids together and then over the next couple decades that started to dissolve and he started to take a look at like how does this affect the boys who are being raised by a grandmother or a mother and he did some research on this and came up with some real interesting research and here's what he found that a boy raised primarily in the company of women tends to have two reactions to women as they grow up.

00:45:10.425 --> 00:45:21.849
The first reaction is when a woman barks or barks, they push back against it. They're aggressive like I will not have a woman telling me what to do.

00:45:21.849 --> 00:45:39.577
